  "caption": "Cinematic chamber folk ballad blended with slow-burn indie rock. Fingerpicked steel-string acoustic guitar and warm cello, a steady piano ostinato, soft brushed drums and a slow deep kick that move with the vocal at the same slow tempo, no fast breakbeats. The verses stay sparse and intimate with guitar, cello and piano; in every chorus the drums, strings and electric guitar swell in layer by layer; the bridge drops back to guitar and voice; the final chorus is the widest and fullest; the outro returns to the fingerpicked guitar alone. Warm close-miked female lead vocal, unhurried phrasing, every word sung clearly, clear English diction. Wooden, earthy, tender, quietly strong, cinematic",
  "seed": 7,
  "lyrics": "[Intro]\n\n[Verse 1]\nHigh on the hill where the wind has its way\nA thin little tree learned to bend and to stay\nDown in the dark where nobody goes\nThe roots kept on walking to where water flows\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nYou keep the shaking on the inside\nSo the leaves won't give you away\n\n[Chorus]\nStill you stand when the wind is high\nNobody sees how the summers ran dry\nSome years you had to grow twice\nYou've got more rings than years\nMore rings than years\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe rain makes no promises, clouds pass you by\nSo you weigh every branch that you send to the sky\nYou never wait for kinder weather\nYou reach for light, however slow\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nYou keep the shaking on the inside\nSo the leaves won't give you away\n\n[Chorus]\nStill you stand when the wind is high\nNobody sees how the summers ran dry\nSome years you had to grow twice\nYou've got more rings than years\nMore rings than years\n\n[Bridge]\nBirds come and go with the turning year\nNobody stays to read what's written here\nI'd rather count the rings with you\nAnd learn the cost of everything\n\n[Final Chorus]\nStill you stand when the wind is high\nNow I can see how the summers ran dry\nSome years you had to grow twice\nYou've got more rings than years\nMore rings than years\n\n[Outro]\nMore rings than years\nAnd still you grow",
